The Amidah blessing for peace is called Sim Shalom (“Grant Peace”). It is the final blessing of the Amidah. Here is a clear English version:

Amidah – Prayer for Peace (Sim Shalom)

Grant peace, goodness, and blessing,
grace, kindness, and compassion
to us and to all Israel, Your people.

Bless us, our Father, all of us as one,
with the light of Your presence.

Blessed are You, Lord,
who blesses His people Israel with peace.
================================================================

Slightly expanded traditional-style translation:

Grant peace, goodness, and blessing,
grace, kindness, and mercy
to us and to all Your people Israel.

Bless us, our Father, all of us together
with the light of Your presence;
for by that light You have given us
the Torah of life, love of kindness,
righteousness, blessing, compassion, life, and peace.

Blessed are You, Lord,
who blesses His people Israel with peace.
